Most leads are already covered by renamed hooks, shared factories, or generated state tables. I found one real parity issue: `HangingSignItem.canPlace` delegates wall-hanging signs to `WallHangingSignBlock.canPlace`, including the axis-compatible neighboring hanging-sign chain check; the live Rust sign placement path currently accepts any tagged sign as support. I’m wiring that validation into the existing `SignBlock::can_place_at` call site and adding a pure unit test for its direction mapping.
