     4	//! `RandomStrollGoal` and every goal that overrides its `getPosition()` picks a destination
     5	//! through these, so a goal ported without them ends up with an ad-hoc offset that ignores
     6	//! build height, home restriction, navmesh stability and pathfinding malus. The three iron
     7	//! golem goals (`MoveTowardsTargetGoal`, `MoveBackToVillageGoal`,
     8	//! `GolemRandomStrollInVillageGoal`) all need them, so they live here rather than being
     9	//! re-approximated per goal.
