One real parity issue is inside the “inlined” target-search lead: Rust was using a spherical center-radius scan, while vanilla’s `getTargetSearchArea` expands the mob’s bounding box into an AABB before filtering candidates. I’ll correct that existing live caller (no new dead API), then record the lead as inlined with the caller named.
