I found two live, source-backed behavior gaps in the existing handlers tied to this worklist: vehicle movement currently accepts invalid coordinates/rotations and updates state even when the client is not loaded or has no vehicle, while player-input handling does not refresh the idle-action timer after a loaded client’s input. Both handlers are invoked from the existing packet dispatch, so I’m wiring only those fixes; the listed `type` leads themselves remain generated packet identity, not new Rust methods.
