    feat(parity): round 13 lane C coverage pass across entity, block, and inventory modules
    
    Adds and fills out method coverage across living/mob/player entity code,
    barrel/lectern/dispenser/sign/sculk-shrieker block behaviour, inventory
    screen handlers, and world loot/random-sequence generation, citing the
    26.2 decompile per method.
    
    Fixes surfaced during gating:
    - world/loot.rs: random_sequence_seed's xor constant now uses hex
      notation (clippy::decimal_bitwise_operands, pedantic).
    - signs.rs: click_command's new test used the legacy camelCase
      "clickEvent" JSON key; Style's click_event field matches vanilla's
      Style.java:622 codec key "click_event" (snake_case) - fixed the test,
      not the code.
    - redstone/dispenser.rs: sulfur_cube test asserted Item::STONE is not
      in minecraft:sulfur_cube_swallowable, but the generated tag data
      (crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/tag.rs) shows stone genuinely is
      a member alongside tnt - swapped the negative case to diamond, which
      is not in the tag.
    - slot.rs, signs.rs, sculk_shrieker.rs, living.rs, entity/mod.rs:
      clippy fixes (pass-by-value cleanup, needless-late-init, const fn,
      excessive-bools) and moved a test module that had been inserted
      mid-file back to the end of the file.
