   250	/// `NearestVisibleLivingEntities` (`memory/NearestVisibleLivingEntities.java:14-71`).
   251	///
   252	/// The living entities a mob saw on its last scan, nearest first
   253	/// (`NearestLivingEntitySensor.java:21`), each flagged with whether line of sight existed at
   254	/// scan time.
   255	///
   256	/// DEVIATION: vanilla computes visibility lazily per query through a per-scan cached
   257	/// predicate (`NearestVisibleLivingEntities.java:26-28`) that re-tests
   258	/// `Sensor.isEntityTargetable`; this port evaluates the flag once during the sensor scan and
   259	/// stores it, because the flag's inputs (positions, blocks between) are exactly what the scan
   260	/// already read. Both forms are allowed up to one 20-tick scan interval of staleness by
   261	/// vanilla's own design (`sensing/Sensor.java:14`). A despawned entity's `Weak` fails to
   262	/// upgrade and is skipped at query time, matching the module-wide weak-reference rule.
   263	#[derive(Clone, Default)]
   264	pub struct NearestVisibleLivingEntities {
   265	    entities: Vec<(Weak<dyn EntityBase>, bool)>,
   266	}
   267	
   268	impl NearestVisibleLivingEntities {
   269	    /// `NearestVisibleLivingEntities.empty()` (`NearestVisibleLivingEntities.java:31-33`).
